    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 6; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many books did Joseph and Sarah have altogether before Joseph lost any? Sarah has 10 books. Joseph had three times as many books as Sarah.\"},{\"turn\":2,\"user_message\":\"Wait, I made a mistake. Sarah has 9 books.\"},{\"turn\":3,\"user_message\":\"Actually, that was wrong. Joseph had twice as many books as Sarah.\"},{\"turn\":4,\"user_message\":\"Oh, I forgot to mention: Joseph's friend lives in a town three miles away.\"},{\"turn\":5,\"user_message\":\"Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many books did Joseph have before he gave 3 books to his friend? Also, here's some relevant info: Before giving the books to his friend, Joseph placed them in a blue box.\"},{\"turn\":6,\"user_message\":\"Here's another detail: the book exchange happened on a Saturday afternoon.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
