  "task_assistant_messages": [
    "Sarah had 10 books.\n\nJoseph had three times as many:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 10 = 30\n\\]\n\nTogether, before Joseph lost any books:\n\n\\[\n30 + 10 = 40\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{40\\text{ books}}\n\\]",
    "Sarah has 9 books.\n\nJoseph had three times as many:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 9 = 27\n\\]\n\nTogether:\n\n\\[\n9 + 27 = 36\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36\\text{ books}}\n\\]",
    "Sarah has 9 books.\n\nJoseph had twice as many:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 9 = 18\n\\]\n\nTogether, they had:\n\n\\[\n9 + 18 = 27\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27\\text{ books}}\n\\]",
    "The friend’s distance does not affect the number of books.\n\nSarah has 9 books, and Joseph has twice as many:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 9 = 18\n\\]\n\nTogether:\n\n\\[\n9 + 18 = 27\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27\\text{ books}}\n\\]",
    "Joseph had **18 books before giving 3 books away**. The blue box does not change the number of books.\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 9 = 18\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18\\text{ books}}\n\\]",
    "The day and time of the exchange do not affect the number of books.\n\nJoseph had twice as many books as Sarah:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 9 = 18\n\\]\n\nSo, before giving 3 books to his friend, Joseph had:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18\\text{ books}}\n\\]",
